          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#nuclear_binding Nuclear binding
          %p
            Together with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-meson"} sigma-meson
            the omega is responsible for most of the long-range
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interaction"} interaction
            between
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+nuclear+force"} strong nuclear force
            between them (as modeled by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Walecka+model"} Walecka model
            and
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+hadrodynamics"} quantum hadrodynamics
          %h3#couplings Couplings
          %h4#TheOmega3PiCoupling
            The
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            = succeed "-coupling" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3 \pi
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interaction"} interaction
            term of the omega-meson three
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pions"} pions
            is, in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mi μ
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\omega_\mu B^\mu
          %p
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+anomaly"} chirally anomalous
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryon+current"} baryon current
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi tr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi d
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi d
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi d
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \coloneqq \star tr( (U^{-1} d U) \wedge (U^{-1} d U) \wedge (U^{-1} d U) )
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is the exponential of the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pion"} pion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
            (
            %a{:href => "#AdkinsNappi84"}> Adkins-Nappi 84, (1) and (2)
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#ParkVento09"} Park-Vento 09, (5.5.43) and above (5.5.50)
          %p
            This gives a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decay+mode"} decay mode
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi π
                    %mo +
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %msup
                    %mi π
                    %mo −
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %msup
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\omega \to \pi^+ + \pi^- + \pi^0
          %p
            (the “charged decay”, e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Rudaz84"} Rudaz 84, (2)
          %p
            Or rather, this is the direct (contact term) decay. The net process
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo →
                  %mn 3
                  %mi π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega \to 3 \pi
            is dominated by the successive decay
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo →
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo +
                  %mi π
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\omega \to \rho + \pi
                  \\to
                  (2 \pi) + \pi
          %h4#TheOmegaRhoPiCoupling
            The
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            = succeed "-coupling" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
          %p
            Then there is an
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/omega-meson"} ω
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rho-meson"} ρ
            = succeed "-coupling" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pion"} π
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+perturbation+theory"} chiral
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW-term"} WZW-term
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi ω
                      %mi ρ
                      %mi π
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mrow
                      %mi μ
                      %mi ν
                      %mi κ
                      %mi λ
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi μ
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mi ν
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi κ
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi λ
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  g_{\omega \rho \pi}
                  \\epsilon^{\mu \nu \kappa \lambda}
                  \\partial_\mu \omega_\nu  \partial_\kappa \rho_\lambda \cdot \pi
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Renard69"} Renard 69
            %a{:href => "#MeissnerKaiserWeise87"} Meissner-Kaiser-Weise 87, (2.18)
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#VolkovEbertNagy97"} Volkov-Ebert-Nagy 97, p. 12
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#GuettaSinger00"} Guetta-Singer 00, (1)
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Kaiser00"} Kaiser 00, (12)
            %a{:href => "#GKSY03"} GKSY 03, (1)
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#GudinoSanchez12"} Gudino-Sanchez 12, (1)
          %h4#the_radiative_decays The radiative decays
          %p Then there is the “neutral decay”
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo +
                  %mi γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\omega \to \pi^0 + \gamma
          %p
            seen in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
            as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi ω
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                          %msup
                            %mi π
                            %mn 0
                          %mo +
                          %mi γ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                          %mi γ
                          %mo +
                          %mi γ
                          %mo +
                          %mi γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  \\omega &amp; \to \pi^0 + \gamma
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \to \gamma + \gamma + \gamma
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Nambu57"}> Nambu 57, (a)
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FFHNR67"} FFHNR 67
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Dolinsky89"} Dolinsky et al. 89, (5)
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pion"}> pion
              ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rho-meson"} rho-meson
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-meson" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
          %ul
            %li#Nambu57
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoichiro+Nambu"}> Yoichiro Nambu
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Possible Existence of a Heavy Neutral Meson
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRev.106.1366"} doi:10.1103/PhysRev.106.1366
          %p as reviewed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jun+John+Sakurai"}> Jun John Sakurai
                , p. 48-49 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Currents and Mesons
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.press.uchicago.edu/ucp/books/book/chicago/C/bo3622598.html"} ISBN: 9780226733838
              %p
                (in the context of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+meson+dominance"} vector meson dominance
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/?title=Omega_meson"} Omega meson
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              Reinhard Alkofer, H. Reinhardt, H. Weigel, U. Zuckert,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Isoscalar vector meson omega in the Nambu-Jona-Lasinio soliton
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/343052"} spire:343052
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(93)91719-4"} doi:10.1016/0370-2693(93)91719-4
          %p Phenomenology:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Cheng-Qun Pang, Ya-Rong Wang, Jing-Fu Hu, Tian-Jie Zhang, Xiang Liu,
