                      In-medium modified energy-momentum tensor form factors of the nucleon within the framework of a
                      = succeed "-" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi π
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
                      = succeed "-" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi ρ
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} omgea
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omgea
                      soliton model
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1402.0161"} arXiv:1402.0161
              %li
                %p
                  Yongseok Oh,
                  %em Skyrmions with vector mesons revisited
                  (
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1402.2821"}> arXiv:1402.2821
                  )
            %p See also
            %ul
              %li
                Ki-Hoon Hong, Ulugbek Yakhshiev, Hyun-Chul Kim,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Modification of hyperon masses in nuclear matter
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.06504"} arXiv:1806.06504
            %p Review:
            %ul
              %li#Kaiser00
                %p
                  Roland Kaiser,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Anomalies and WZW-term of two-flavour QCD
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0011377"} arXiv:hep-ph/0011377
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/537600"} spire:537600
              %li#Holzwarth05
                %p
                  Gottfried Holzwarth, Section 2.3 of:
                  %em Electromagnetic Form Factors of the Nucleon in Chiral Soliton Models
                  (
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0511194"}> arXiv:hep-ph/0511194
                  ), Chapter 2 in:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Multifaceted+Skyrmion"} The Multifaceted Skyrmion
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9710"} doi:10.1142/9710
              %li
                %p
                  Yongseok Oh,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Skyrmions with vector mesons: Single Skyrmion and baryonic matter
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/OhSkyrmionsWithVectorMesons.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %p
              Combination of the
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/omega-meson"} omega
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rho+meson"} rho
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrme+model"} Skyrme model
              with the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bag+model+of+quark+confinement"} bag model of quark confinement
            %ul
              %li
                H. Takashita, S. Yoro, H. Toki,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Chiral bag plus skyrmion hybrid model with vector mesons for nucleon
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0375-9474(88)90555-6"} doi:10.1016/0375-9474(88)90555-6
            %h4#inclusion_of_the_meson_3
              Inclusion of the
              = succeed "-meson" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            %p
              Inclusion of the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-meson"} sigma-meson
            %ul
              %li
                Thomas D. Cohen,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Explicit
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi σ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                    meson, topology, and the large-
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi N
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
                    limit of the Skyrmion
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.37.3344"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.37.3344
            %p
              For analysis of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neutron+star"} neutron star
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equation+of+state"} equation of state
            %ul
              %li
                David Alvarez-Castillo, Alexander Ayriyan, Gergely Gábor Barnaföldi, Hovik Grigorian, Péter Pósfay,
                %em
                  Studying the parameters of the extended
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi σ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ω
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
                  model for neutron star matter
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.03676"}> arXiv:2006.03676
                )
          %h3#couplings_2 Couplings
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/omega-meson"} omega-meson
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interactions"} interactions
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decay+modes"} decay modes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Stanley M. Flatté, Darrell O. Huwe, Joseph J. Murray, Janice Button-Shafer, Frank T. Solmitz, M. Lynn Stevenson, and Charles Wohl,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Decay Properties of the
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ω
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
                    Meson
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRev.145.1050"} doi:10.1103/PhysRev.145.1050
            %li#FFHNR67
              %p
                M. Feldman, W. Frati, R. Gleeson, J. Halpern, M. Nussbaum, S. Richert,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Neutral Decay of the
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ω
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
                    Meson
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRev.159.1219"} doi10.1103/PhysRev.159.1219
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/52556"} spire:52556
            %li
              %p
                W. Deinet A. Menzione H.Müller, H. M.Staudenmaier, S.Buniatov, D.Schmitt,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Neutral decay modes of the
                    = succeed "-meson" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi ω
                              %mn 0
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega^0
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(69)90479-1"} doi:10.1016/0370-2693(69)90479-1
            %li#Renard69
              %p
                F. M. Renard,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    The reaction
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi e
                            %mo +
                          %msup
                            %mi e
                            %mo −
                          %mo →
                          %msup
                            %mi π
                            %mn 0
                          %mo +
                          %mi ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi π
                            %mo +
                          %msup
                            %mi π
                            %mo −
                          %msup
                            %mi π
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e^+ e^-  \to \pi^0 + \omega(\pi^+ \pi^- \pi^0)
                    and the
                    = succeed "-" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi ω
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
                    = succeed "-" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi ρ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi π
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
                    coupling
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02758844"} doi:10.1007/BF02758844
            %li#VolkovEbertNagy97
              %p
                M. K. Volkov, D. Ebert, M. Nagy,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Excited pions,
                    = succeed "-" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi ρ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
                    = succeed "-mesons" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi ω
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi SU
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ×
                          %mi SU
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2) \times SU(2)
                    Lagrangian
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/9705334"} arXiv:hep-ph/9705334
            %li#Dolinsky89
              %p
                S. I. Dolinsky, et al.,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Radiative Decays of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ρ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
                    and
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ω
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
                    Mesons
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/264694"} spire:264694
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01557655"} doi:10.1007/BF01557655
            %li
              %p
                J. T. Dakin, M. G. Hauser, M. N. Kreisler, R. E. Mischke,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Measurement of the Branching Ratios for ω Neutral Decays
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.6.2321"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.6.2321
            %li#GuettaSinger00
              %p
                Dafne Guetta, Paul Singer,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ω
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
                    \-
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ρ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
                    Mixing and the
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ω
                          %mo →
                          %mi π
                          %mi π
                          %mi γ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega \to \pi \pi \gamma
                    Decay
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0005059"} arXiv:hep-ph/0005059
            %li#Kaiser00
              %p
                Roland Kaiser, equation (12) of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Anomalies and WZW-term of two-flavour QCD
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0011377"} arXiv:hep-ph/0011377
            %li#GKSY03
              %p
                A. Gokalp, A. Kucukarslan, S. Solmaz, O. Yilmaz,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi σ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                    \-Meson and
                    = succeed "-" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi ω
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ρ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
                    mixing effects in
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ω
                          %mo →
                          %msup
                            %mi π
                            %mo +
                          %msup
                            %mi π
                            %mo −
                          %mi γ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega \to \pi^+ \pi^- \gamma
                    decay
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0306044"} arXiv:hep-ph/0306044
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeffrey+Harvey"}> Jeffrey Harvey
                , Christopher T. Hill, Richard J. Hill, Section II.B of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Standard Model Gauging of the WZW Term: Anomalies, Global Currents and pseudo-Chern-Simons Interactions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0712.1230"} arXiv:0712.1230
            %li
              %p
                S. Leupold, M. F. M. Lutz,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Hadronic three-body decays of light vector mesons
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0807.4686"} arXiv:0807.4686
            %li
              %p
                Florian Jonas,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Measurement of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ω
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
                    and
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi η
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
                    mesons via their three pion decay with ALICE in pp collisions at
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msqrt
                            %mi s
                          %mo =
                          %mi t
                          %mi TeV
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sqrt{s} = t TeV
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://cds.cern.ch/record/2653176"} cds:2653176
          %h3#in_holographic_qcd In holographic QCD
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/omega-meson"} omega-meson
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"} holographic QCD
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten-Sakai-Sugimoto+model"}> Witten-Sakai-Sugimoto model
            ):
          %ul
            %li#SakaiSugimoto05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tadakatsu+Sakai"}> Tadakatsu Sakai
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shigeki+Sugimoto"} Shigeki Sugimoto
              = succeed "," do
                %em More on a holographic dual of QCD
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0507073"} arXiv:hep-th/0507073
          %h3#mediating_baryon_interaction Mediating baryon interaction
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-mesons"} sigma-mesons
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/omega-mesons"} omega-mesons
            mediating
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryon"} baryon
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interaction"} interaction
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"} holographic QCD
            via
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D3-D7+brane+intersections"} D3-D7 brane intersections
          %ul
            %li
              Anatoly Dymarsky, Dmitry Melnikov,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Sonnenschein"} Jacob Sonnenschein
              = succeed "," do
                %em Attractive Holographic Baryons
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1012.1616"} arXiv:1012.1616
